        {
          "type": "note",
          "tone": "warning",
          "title": "Gotchas",
          "text": "- Colours are adjectives: they agree with the noun (une jupe bleue, un pull bleu, des sandales vertes, des chaussettes blanches) and come after it. English puts them before: “a blue skirt”.\n- Orange and marron do not change (des tennis orange), because they are names of things (an orange, a chestnut). Rose and violet are regular: des jupes roses.\n- Colours ending in -e (rouge, jaune, beige, orange) look the same in masculine and feminine: un pull rouge, une jupe rouge. Only add -s in the plural: des pulls rouges.\n- French sizes are numbers: in a shop in France, a 38 is a medium. For shoes, la pointure is the shoe size, la taille the clothes size.\n- Un jean is masculine singular in French: un jean bleu (a pair of jeans). Un pantalon too: un pantalon noir. English “trousers / pants” are plural; French is singular.\n- Chaussures, chaussettes, bottes, sandales, baskets, tennis are plural nouns in French, and pair is often implied: une paire de chaussures."
