              "[e]",
              "relâché, bouche ouverte",
              "Le déjeuner. Je me lève. Chez moi. Dîner."
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "note",
          "tone": "tip",
          "title": "How to hear it",
          "text": "- [i] is the tight smile, like English “ee” in “see”, but shorter and without a glide: midi, ici, Paris, il.\n- [e] is like the vowel in “day” but without the final y glide: pure, no “ey”. Spelled é, er, ez, ai: déjeuner, dîner, lever, chez, j'ai.\n- Don't turn é into “ay” as in English “café”: say ka-fé with a short, steady sound.\n- Final -er (déjeuner, dîner, habiller) sounds just [e]: the r is silent. Same for -ez (chez, vous essayez)."
        },
        {
          "type": "phrases",
